      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(firecrawl): require own legacy provider config entries",
        "body": "### What Problem This Solves\n\nFirecrawl legacy web config lookup used inherited `firecrawl` properties from `tools.web.search` and `tools.web.fetch` as if they were explicit user config entries. A prototype-provided nested provider config could override the normal env/default behavior at the Firecrawl boundary.\n\n### Why This Change Was Made\n\nUse own-property checks for the legacy nested Firecrawl entries while preserving the existing plugin config precedence and resolver shape.\n\n### User Impact\n\nFirecrawl only consumes legacy web config when users actually define the `firecrawl` entry on that config object. Inherited entries are ignored, so unset config falls back to the existing env/default path. Existing explicit own legacy config and plugin-owned config precedence are preserved.\n\n### Evidence\n\nExact head: `e56723d22efcf44c0c817cdf17f8c04092be6bb8`\n\nBehavior covered by `extensions/firecrawl/src/config.own-entries.test.ts`:\n\n- resolver-level proof for both legacy sibling surfaces: `tools.web.search.firecrawl` and `tools.web.fetch.firecrawl`;\n- actual `runFirecrawlSearch` client path with inherited legacy `apiKey`/`baseUrl`, proving the request uses `https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2/search` plus `Bearer env-search-key` instead of the inherited values;\n- actual `runFirecrawlScrape` client path with inherited legacy `apiKey`/`baseUrl`, proving the request uses `https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2/scrape` plus `Bearer env-fetch-key` instead of the inherited values.\n\nValidation run:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/firecrawl/src/config.own-entries.test.ts` (4 tests passed)\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/firecrawl/src/config.own-entries.test.ts`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint --threads=1 extensions/firecrawl/src/config.own-entries.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.extensions.test.json --incremental false --pretty false`\n- `env -u OPENAI_API_KEY -u OPENAI_ORG_ID -u OPENAI_PROJECT_ID .agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` (exit 0, no findings)\n\nOverlap note: #103492 touches the same Firecrawl files plus broader config surfaces. This PR remains the narrower Firecrawl-only patch with direct client-path regression coverage for both Firecrawl legacy surfaces.\n",
        "branch": "alix/firecrawl-own-legacy-provider-config",
        "head_sha": "e56723d22efcf44c0c817cdf17f8c04092be6bb8",
